

Data model for the proton manifold

Quark state

Positions:(\vec{x}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3), (i = 1..3)

Momenta:(\vec{p}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3)

Color charges:(c_i \in {\text{red, green, blue}}) or encoded as one‑hot / vector

Gluon field

Field values:(G(\vec{x})) sampled on a grid or basis

Intensity / flux:local energy density, field strength

Effective fields

Confinement potential:e.g., linear or harmonic potential between quarks

Mass/energy density:distribution inside the proton volume

Constraints

color neutrality

baryon number

symmetry constraints (e.g., SU(3) structure encoded abstractly)

Software blueprint — UnifiedProton class

class QuarkState:
    def __init__(self, positions, momenta, colors):
        self.positions = positions  # shape: (3, 3)
        self.momenta = momenta      # shape: (3, 3)
        self.colors = colors        # shape: (3,)

class GluonField:
    def __init__(self, field_values, grid):
        self.field_values = field_values  # e.g., (Nx, Ny, Nz)
        self.grid = grid                  # coordinates

class EffectiveFields:
    def __init__(self, confinement_potential, energy_density):
        self.confinement_potential = confinement_potential
        self.energy_density = energy_density

class Constraints:
    def __init__(self, color_neutrality, baryon_number, symmetry_score):
        self.color_neutrality = color_neutrality
        self.baryon_number = baryon_number
        self.symmetry_score = symmetry_score

Now the Unified Proton Equation:

class UnifiedProton:
    def __init__(self, phi_strategy):
        self.phi = phi_strategy  # fusion operator

    def compute_U(self, quark_state, gluon_field, eff_fields, constraints):
        """
        U(P) = Φ(Q, G, F, C)
        Returns a unified proton state vector / tensor.
        """
        return self.phi(quark_state, gluon_field, eff_fields, constraints)

Fusion operator Φ — your design lever

You can define different Φ strategies:

def phi_energy_weighted(quark_state, gluon_field, eff_fields, constraints):
    # Sketch: combine into a single feature vector
    # (you’ll later refine this into something more physical or learned)
    features = []

    # Quark positions & momenta
    features.extend(quark_state.positions.flatten())
    features.extend(quark_state.momenta.flatten())

    # Simple aggregates of gluon field
    features.append(gluon_field.field_values.mean())
    features.append(gluon_field.field_values.var())

    # Effective fields
    features.append(eff_fields.confinement_potential.mean())
    features.append(eff_fields.energy_density.mean())

    # Constraints
    features.append(constraints.color_neutrality)
    features.append(constraints.baryon_number)
    features.append(constraints.symmetry_score)

    return features  # or np.array(features)

Then:

unified = UnifiedProton(phi_strategy=phi_energy_weighted)
U = unified.compute_U(Q, G, F, C)

